{"name":"First Love","hex":"#cf758a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"first love","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One's first experience of the feeling of romantic love.","The first person to be the object of one's romantic affection."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/first_love"}],"entries":[{"title":"First Love (1921 film)","blocks":[{"text":"First Love is a 1921 American silent romantic comedy film produced by the Realart Pictures Corporation and distributed through the related Paramount Pictures. It stars Constance Binney and was directed by Maurice Campbell. Warner Baxter has one of his earliest screen portrayals here. Only the first reel of this film is known to survive at the Museum of Modern Art."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/First_Love_%281921%29_-_1.jpg/330px-First_Love_%281921%29_-_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Love_(1921_film)"},{"title":"First Love (1939 film)","blocks":[{"text":"First Love is a 1939 American musical film directed by Henry Koster and starring Deanna Durbin. An adaptation of the fairy tale Cinderella, the film is about orphan Constance \"Connie\" Harding who is sent to live with her wealthy aunt Grace and uncle James after graduating from boarding school. Her life is made difficult by her snobby cousin Barbara who arranges that she stay home while the rest of the family attends a major social ball. With the help of James, Connie makes it to the ball, where she meets and falls in love with Barbara's boyfriend Ted Drake. The film received Academy Award nominations for Best Art Direction and Best Music at the 12th Academy Awards. It was on a preliminary list of submissions from the studios for Best Cinematography (Black-and-White) but was not nominated."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b5/First_Love_1939_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Love_(1939_film)"},{"title":"First Love (Hikaru Utada album)","blocks":[{"text":"First Love is the debut Japanese-language studio album by Japanese-American recording artist Hikaru Utada, released on March 10, 1999, by Eastworld."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Hikaru_Utada_-_First_Love.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Love_(Hikaru_Utada_album)"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/First_Love_%281921%29_-_5.jpg/120px-First_Love_%281921%29_-_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/First_Love_%281921%29_-_5.jpg/250px-First_Love_%281921%29_-_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/First_Love_%281921%29_-_5.jpg/120px-First_Love_%281921%29_-_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirst_Love_(1921)_-_5.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/First_Love_%281921%29_-_6.jpg/120px-First_Love_%281921%29_-_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi